{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Sword clash",
  "description": "Two steel blades meet edge to edge in a stone courtyard: a harsh bite, a clank and a ring, not a chime. First the edges bite, a brief broadband crunch of steel on steel. With it the attacker's long blade is set ringing, struck near its tip and chattering twice more against the other edge: a bright, crowded, beating cluster of high overtones, with no single bell note under it. A hair later the defender's blade, gripped hard, answers with the clank, lower, dented and quickly dead. Then the edges grind along each other to the guards, a gritty 'shing' that slows down. The walls give it a short hard slap, and the attacker's blade sings on after the rest.",
  "tags": [
    "weapon",
    "sword",
    "clash",
    "clang",
    "metal",
    "blade",
    "parry",
    "melee",
    "impact",
    "steel"
  ],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 15,
  "tracks": [
